<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Greenland Trading Department</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1776">1776</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Kongelige Grønlandske Handel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a> Trading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a> (Kongelige Grønlandske Handel) was a Danish state enterprise founded in 1776 that held a monopoly on trade with Greenland. It ran the trading stations, supplied the settlements and bought seal products and fish, and for long periods also administered the colonies, keeping Greenland closed to outsiders until its monopoly ended in 1950.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-greenland-trading-department.jpg" alt="Royal Greenland Trading Department" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: N. J. Bredal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gr%C3%B8nlandske_Handels_Plads_(1810).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
